% ========================================================================
% C11 re-scoping probe — separated-credential design (must stay SAT)
% ========================================================================
% The design the paper PRESCRIBES as the remedy for a C11 revocation-cadence
% mismatch: put the two claims in two different credentials. This probe takes
% the canonical CSOK decomposition unchanged (three credentials, one per
% claim, all three credential subjects tracing the same domain Subject
% `Applicant`) and marks two claims that already live in SEPARATE credentials
% with mismatched cadence:
%   has_children_claim (FamilyStatusCred) -> StaticRevocation
%   earns_claim        (IncomeCred)       -> DynamicRevocation
%
% There is no bundling here and nothing to repair, so `revocation_mismatch`
% must NOT fire. Expected: `Model is consistent` under `check -k`.
%
% Built for the K-003 stress-test finding F1 (2026-08-03): under the
% pre-restriction `colocated_step`, the alignment disjunct made ANY two
% credential subjects of one domain subject co-located, so this probe was
% INCONSISTENT — the predicate flagged the prescribed remedy as the disease.
% Companion control: probe_c11_separated_design_control.problem (same design,
% single cadence).
%
% No governance markers and no `governance_conflict` import: the CSOK
% governance conflict is a different constraint (C8) and would mask the C11
% verdict.
% ========================================================================

import vc_metamodel.
import revocation_mismatch.
import csok_instance.


% === Revocation-cadence markers (mismatched, but in separate credentials) ===

declare static_family, dynamic_income.

StaticRevocation(static_family).
StaticRevocation::target(static_family, has_children_claim).
DynamicRevocation(dynamic_income).
DynamicRevocation::target(dynamic_income, earns_claim).

% Close markers
!exists(StaticRevocation::new).
!exists(DynamicRevocation::new).

% 22 nodes from csok_instance (7 DCL + 12 CSL + 3 FSL) + 2 markers
scope node = 24.
